        "id": 1112679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-04T00:05:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are checking `service.sendBroadcast()` is called to check the state transition happened, but this can lead to future error. \n\nFor example, one day BassClientStateMachine starts to send some other broadcasts before state is changing, then this test is affected.\n\nDid the checking `enter()` not work?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 343,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 344,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "aa5f69a47ea37b973c6ad58827cb9a329871b9ed",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8ba70c7_98666bbe",
        "filename": "android/app/tests/unit/src/com/android/bluetooth/bass_client/BassClientStateMachineTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 344,
      "author": {
        "id": 1953983
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-07T06:05:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Checking `enter()` require the inner state classes to be spied, i.e. `spy(state)`, but it will cause error because of the interaction with `addState(state)`. There are ways to work around, but they are more complicated and worse for readability.\n\nfor the checking `service.sendBroadcast()`, I simply follow what Sungsoo did in here: https://source.corp.google.com/android-internal/packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/tests/unit/src/com/android/bluetooth/hap/HapClientStateMachineTest.java;l\u003d379;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1;rcl\u003db3370acc279c39e98823a2dbb9835fe0db615579?q\u003dsendMessageAndVerifyTransition. Also, as he mentioned before in a sync up, if there is any changed behavior that break the test, we can fix the test later accordingly.",
      "parentUuid": "7399b5e3_0b4a5672",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 343,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 344,
        "endChar": 55
